 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No dead animal, blood or pig drawn: a book for «فيما أوحي إلي», geometric for «فإن ربك غفور رحيم». 145:1-7 carries As-Sa'di's note that other things are also forbidden (predators…), and 145:8-11 Al-Muyassar's context «مما تذكرون أنه حُرِّم من الأنعام», so the list is not read as exhaustive. Al-Muyassar's first-person «حرمَّنا» (146) not used; 146:27-28 not glossed. STAGING v4: c1 (145): believers in a market of grain and fruit; the book plate stands for the revelation (145:6-11; no plate starts on «قل», the Prophet is not shown). Nothing forbidden is drawn (no dead animal, blood, pig or slaughter); the believers shake their heads on 145:15 and 145:23 (refusing what is impure). For the one compelled by hunger (Al-Muyassar) a poor man appears sitting on 145:31, without any gesture; geometric for «فإن ربك غفور رحيم». No purse is given (the ruling is food). c2 (146): the people the ruling was given to (3 faceless figures, no women) in a market, with a camel for the animals of undivided hoof (As-Sa'di: like camels) on 146:6; no cattle, sheep, fat or meat is drawn and nothing is acted for the recompense of their transgression; a seal plate for «وإنا لصادقون»."
 },
